From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] NextBSD: dwmmc: poll the controller while dumping

dwmmc_request() starts a command and returns, relying on the controller
interrupt to finish it. At panic time the scheduler is stopped and the
interrupt is never delivered, so an mmcsd dump on a dwmmc host hangs.
Mirror sdhci_generic_request(): when dumping, call dwmmc_intr() directly
and spin until the request is done. Also skip the bus_busy wait in
dwmmc_acquire_host() while dumping, since msleep() returns at once with
the scheduler stopped and the bus owner can no longer run.

No struct or header changes (nextbsd-kernel#226).
---
 sys/dev/mmc/host/dwmmc.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/dev/mmc/host/dwmmc.c b/sys/dev/mmc/host/dwmmc.c
index a422d86d6..b56374d71 100644
--- a/sys/dev/mmc/host/dwmmc.c
+++ b/sys/dev/mmc/host/dwmmc.c
@@ -1255,6 +1255,19 @@ dwmmc_request(device_t brdev, device_t reqdev, struct mmc_request *req)
 	dwmmc_next_operation(sc);
 	DWMMC_UNLOCK(sc);
 
+	/*
+	 * While dumping, the scheduler is stopped and interrupts are not
+	 * delivered, so the request would never complete and the mmcsd
+	 * dump routine would wait forever. Poll the controller instead,
+	 * the same way sdhci does, until the request has been finished.
+	 */
+	if (dumping) {
+		while (sc->req != NULL) {
+			dwmmc_intr(sc);
+			DELAY(10);
+		}
+	}
+
 	return (0);
 }
 
@@ -1275,7 +1288,11 @@ dwmmc_acquire_host(device_t brdev, device_t reqdev)
 	sc = device_get_softc(brdev);
 
 	DWMMC_LOCK(sc);
-	while (sc->bus_busy)
+	/*
+	 * msleep() returns at once when the scheduler is stopped, so do not
+	 * wait for a bus owner that can no longer run while dumping.
+	 */
+	while (sc->bus_busy && !dumping)
 		msleep(sc, &sc->sc_mtx, PZERO, "dwmmcah", hz / 5);
 	sc->bus_busy++;
 	DWMMC_UNLOCK(sc);
-- 
2.50.0

